    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I know, I know... \"new beginnings\" and all that. But this isn't a storybook. There's no phoenix rising from these ashes. It's just me, a hollow shell of a person, sitting in the mud. I look at my sword, the one I used to defend everything, and the only thing it seems to offer now is a sense of familiarity. It's the only thing in this whole gods-forsaken world that hasn't lied to me or left me. It feels like the only thing that actually understands how much it hurts to be nothing.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
